 "result": "Full suite passes (1562 passed, no failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nFixed the bug in `src/click/_termui_impl.py`: `MaybeStripAnsi` (used by `get_pager_file`/`echo_via_pager`) subclasses `io.TextIOWrapper` wrapping the real stdin/stdout buffer or a pager subprocess's stdin pipe. `TextIOWrapper`'s default `__del__` closes its underlying buffer when garbage collected, which meant that after paging finished, the process's real stdin/stdout (or the pager's pipe) could get closed out from under the rest of the program.\n\nAdded a `__del__` override that calls `self.detach()` instead, matching the existing `_NonClosingTextIOWrapper` pattern already used elsewhere in Click (`_compat.py`) for the same reason. Also added a `CHANGES.rst` entry. Full test suite (1562 tests) passes against the local `src/click`.",
